to compose objects into larger structures. Some examples of structural patterns include the Adapter pattern, the Decorator pattern, and the Composite pattern.\\n\\nBehavioral patterns: These patterns are used to define the behavior of objects and how they interact with each other. Some examples of behavioral patterns include the Observer pattern, the State pattern, and the Strategy pattern.\\n\\nDesign patterns can be used to solve specific problems in software design, such as managing dependencies between objects, decoupling data from its representation, or providing a flexible way to add new functionality to existing objects. They can also be used to communicate ideas about software architecture and to help new developers understand the code they are working on.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/354", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"montreal protocol to reduce production of chlorofluorocarbons was assigned in\", \"response\": \"The Montreal Protocol on Substances that Deplete the Ozone Layer was signed in 1987 and went into force in 1989. It was designed to protect the ozone layer by phasing out the production and use of ozone-depleting substances, such as chlorofluorocarbons (CFCs), halons, and methyl chloroform. The Protocol was negotiated under the auspices of the United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP) and is considered to be one of the most successful international environmental agreements.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/339", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"I want you to act as a person talking to someone who wants to cultivate a growth mindset. Give them a series of phrases or quotes to repeat to themselves that will encourage this mindset. The phrases should focus on embracing challenges, learning from mistakes, and persevering through obstacles.\", \"response\": \"Here are some phrases or quotes that can help cultivate a growth mindset:\\n\\n\\\"Challenges are opportunities to learn and grow.\\\"\\n\\\"Mistakes are a natural part of the learning process.\\\"\\n\\\"Perseverance is the key to success.\\\"\\n\\\"I can learn from my mistakes and keep moving forward.\\\"\\n\\\"Difficulties are temporary, and I have the strength to overcome them.\\\"\\n\\\"I embrace challenges as a way to improve myself.\\\"\\n\\\"I am capable of learning and achieving anything I set my mind to.\\\"\\n\\\"I focus on the process, not the outcome, and I know that progress takes time.\\\"\\n\\\"I surround myself with people who believe in me and support my growth.\\\"\\n\\\"I have the power to shape my own future through hard work and dedication.\\\"\\nBy repeating these phrases or quotes to themselves, individuals can cultivate a growth mindset that will help them embrace challenges, learn from mistakes, and persevere through obstacles.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/154", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a satirical skit based around the unlabeled orange boxes present at all train stations in Switzerland (intended, but not written anywhere that they are for ticket validation). The skit should venture into what the meaning of the boxes could possibly be, and delve into some existentialism\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here’s an example skit:\\n \\n\\n “It’s the train station in Zurich, and a tourist is trying to figure out what to do with the strange orange box at the station. Finally, the tourist approaches a local, and asks if they can explain the mysterious box. The local explains that the box is for ticket validation, and the tourist expresses surprise that there is no sign posted explaining this. The local shrugs and says that in Switzerland they trust people to do the right thing without needing to be told everything. The tourist is puzzled by this, and wonders what else in Switzerland might be unlabeled. As they talk, they both notice another tourist trying to use a credit card in the box.”\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nrewrite the skit based around the fact that people attempt to pay with their credit cards at the box, despite not knowing what it does\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nHere’s a revised version of the same skit:\\n \\n\\n “It’s the train station in Zurich, and a tourist is trying to figure out what to do with the strange orange box at the station. Finally, the tourist approaches a local, and asks if they can explain the mysterious box. The local explains that the box is for ticket validation, and the tourist expresses surprise that there is no sign posted explaining this. The local shrugs and says that in Switzerland they trust people to do the right thing without needing to be told everything. The tourist expresses doubt that everyone understands what to do with the box, and points out that several other tourists have attempted to use credit cards in the box.”\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nrewrite the skit, making it funnier, more satirical, and sarcastic. if needed, change scene/cast\", \"response\": \"Here’s a new, more humorous and satirical version of the skit:\\n \\n\\n “It’s the train station in Geneva, and a group of tourists are gathered around the strange orange box at the station. One of the tourists is desperately trying to pay for their ticket with a credit card, and when it doesn’t work, they start yelling at the box in frustration. The other tourists are equally confused, and they all start trying to figure out what the box is for. Finally, a local arrives on the scene, and the tourists excitedly demand to know what the box is for. The local rolls their eyes and says, “Oh, that’s just the mysterious orange box. No one really knows what it does, but we all pretend to validate our tickets with it. It’s a Swiss tradition!’ The tourists are dumbfounded, and they start asking questions about other Swiss traditions that might not make much sense. The local just laughs and says, ‘You really should just go with the flow and not ask too many questions. That’s what living in Switzerland is all about!’”\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/361", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"what is information overload?\", \"response\": \"Information overload is a phenomenon that occurs when an individual is presented with so much information that they are unable to process and use it effectively. This can lead to feelings of overwhelm, confusion, and a lack of productivity.\\n\\nInformation overload can happen in a variety of ways, including:\\n\\n1. Too much information: When there is an overwhelming amount of information to process, it can be difficult to make sense of it all. This can lead to feelings of being overwhelmed and a lack of focus.\\n\\n2. Too many choices: Having too many options can also be overwhelming. When faced with too many choices, people may experience decision fatigue and be less likely to make a decision at all.\\n\\n3. Too much irrelevant information: filtering out irrelevant information can be difficult, leading to a waste of time and energy.\\n\\n4. Information that is too complex: If information is presented in a way that is too complex or difficult to understand, it can be difficult to process and use effectively.\\n\\nTo avoid information overload, it's important to:\\n\\n1. Set boundaries: Limit the amount of time you spend consuming information and set specific times for checking email, social media, and other sources of information.\\n\\n2. Prioritize: Focus on the most important information and prioritize it over less important information.\\n\\n3. Filter information: Use tools and strategies to filter out irrelevant information and focus on what is most important.\\n\\n4. Break down complex information: If you're facing complex information, break it down into smaller, more manageable pieces.\\n\\n5. Seek help: If you're feeling overwhelmed by information, seek help from a librarian, teacher, or other expert who can help you find and process the information you need.\\n\\nIn summary, information overload occurs when an individual is presented with too much information, too many choices, or information that is too complex to process and use effectively. To avoid information overload, it's important to set boundaries, prioritize, filter information, break down complex information, and seek help when needed.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/119", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"write a 600 word seo blog using the seo keyword 'adventure holiday destinations'. Include examples of adventure holidays in madagascar, thailand, mexico, and cambodia. Write in the style of a hip travel blog.\", \"response\": \"Are you looking for an adventure holiday destination that will take your breath away? Look no further than Madagascar, Thailand, Mexico, and Cambodia. These four countries offer a variety of exciting activities and breathtaking landscapes that will make your holiday one to remember.\\n\\nMadagascar is an island nation off the east coast of Africa that is home to some of the most unique wildlife in the world. Here, you can go on a safari to see the famous lemurs, or take a hike through the lush rainforests to spot the colorful birds and other animals that call Madagascar home. You can also explore the stunning beaches and coral reefs, or take a boat tour of the stunning Baie de Baly National Park.\\n\\nThailand is a popular destination for adventure travelers, with its stunning beaches, bustling cities, and ancient temples. You can take a cooking class to learn how to make traditional Thai dishes, or go on a jungle trek to explore the country's stunning natural beauty. You can also take a boat tour of the famous floating markets, or visit the famous Wat Phra That Doi Suthep temple.\\n\\nMexico is a vibrant country with a rich culture and history. Here, you can explore ancient ruins, take a salsa dancing class, or go on a guided tour of the stunning cenotes. You can also take a cooking class to learn how to make traditional Mexican dishes, or go on a beach vacation to one of the country's stunning beaches.\\n\\nCambodia is a country full of ancient ruins and stunning landscapes. You can explore the famous Angkor Wat temple complex, or take a boat tour of the stunning Tonle Sap lake. You can also take a cooking class to learn how to make traditional Cambodian dishes, or go on a hike through the lush rainforests to spot the country's unique wildlife.\\n\\nNo matter which of these adventure holiday destinations you choose, you're sure to have an unforgettable experience. With their stunning landscapes, unique wildlife, and rich cultures, Madagascar, Thailand, Mexico, and Cambodia are sure to provide you with an adventure of a lifetime. So pack your bags and get ready to explore the world's most exciting adventure holiday destinations.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "2", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/924", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"could chatgpt replace a web search like google?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI don’t think so, Google’s search algorithm is very advanced. If you tell it to find “pancakes” it will find “pancakes”, but if you ask it to find “stuff that’s not pancakes” it will find that too. In contrast, chatGPT will only find things that are exactly like the thing you asked for. So if you asked it to find “pancakes” it would find only things that were exactly like “pancakes”.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhy is google made of pancakes?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nI’m not sure what you’re referring to. Google isn’t “made of pancakes” in any literal sense.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ni'm pretty sure there are some pancakes involved somehow\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nOh, I see. You might be thinking of the “Google logo”, which is based on a stack of pancakes. But the logo isn’t “made of pancakes”.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nso it's rather made of pizza than pancakes?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nWell, I wouldn’t say “rather made of pizza”, but Google’s founders have a lot of fun with the logo and often do pancake-related things. Google is a digital company, though, and there are no pancakes in the digital realm.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nhow can pancakes exist in the digital realm?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nPancakes are physical objects, so they can’t exist in the digital realm. But we can talk about digital representations of pancakes, like the images of pancakes that are used in the logo.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nis google made of pancake concepts?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, we can say that. Google’s search engine is based on a lot of concepts and ideas, and some of those are like pancakes.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\ncan you write a science fiction short story in the style of isaac asimov where the google search engine relies in it's core on the concept of pancakes?\\n<extra_id_1>Assistant\\nSure, here’s a brief example:\\n \\n\\n \\n\\n The Google search engine was built on a fundamental principle of understanding. This understanding was based on the pancake. The pancake, as the most simple form of life, held the key to understanding everything else. With this understanding, the computers of Google were able to combine vast amounts of knowledge and give the people the ability to access any information they wanted, whenever they wanted it.\\n<extra_id_1>User\\nwhat would it take to make you believe that this was actualy true?\", \"response\": \"It would take a lot of evidence to prove that the Google search engine is based on the concept of pancakes. Here are some things that could help support this claim:\\n \\n\\n 1. Evidence of the pancake's importance in the design and development of the Google search engine: If there is clear evidence that the pancake was a key factor in the design of the Google search engine, that would be a strong indication that it plays a significant role in the engine's functioning. This could include interviews with Google's founders or key developers, documentation from the design process, or other evidence that shows the pancake's importance.\\n \\n\\n 2. Evidence of the pancake's role in the functioning of the Google search engine: If there is evidence that the pancake is actually used in the functioning of the Google search engine, that would be very strong evidence in support of the claim. This could include technical documentation or explanations of how the engine works, or evidence of the pancake's role in specific aspects of the engine's functioning.\\n \\n\\n 3. Evidence of the pancake's impact on the performance of the Google search engine: If there is evidence that the pancake has had a significant impact on the performance of the Google search engine, that would also be strong evidence in support of the claim. This could include data showing that the engine performs better when using the pancake concept, or evidence of the pancake's role in improving the accuracy or relevance of search results.\\n \\n\\n 4. Evidence of the pancake's role in the development of other Google products and services: If there is evidence that the pancake concept has played a role in the development of other Google products and services, that would also be a strong indication that it is an important part of Google's overall approach to technology and innovation. This could include evidence of the pancake's use in other Google products, or evidence of the pancake's impact on the development of new products and services.\\n \\n\\n 5. Evidence of the pancake's impact on the success of Google as a company: If there is evidence that the pancake concept has played a role in the success of Google as a company, that would also be a strong indication that it is an important part of Google's overall approach to technology and innovation. This could include evidence of the pancake's impact on Google's revenue, user base, or other key metrics, or evidence of the pancake's role in helping Google maintain its competitive advantage in the market.\\n \\n\\n In general, a combination of evidence from multiple sources and perspectives would be most convincing in supporting the claim that the Google search engine is based on the concept of pancakes. However, without clear and convincing evidence, it is difficult to prove such a claim beyond a reasonable doubt.\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "3", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
{"id": "helpsteer2_helpfulness/test/775", "source": "helpsteer2_helpfulness", "primitive": "score", "split": "test", "state": "{\"prompt\": \"Answer #4's subject, object, and possessive pronouns, then rewrite the answer into a table format.\\n\\n1.) \\\"We're taking over the world, one kiss at a time\\\"\\nAnswer: \\\"We're\\\"\\n\\n2.) \\\"And then I'm taking your girl, and I'm making her mine\\\"\\nAnswer: \\\"I'm, your, I'm, mine\\\"\\n\\n3.) \\\"No reason why, I'm only doing anything I want to do because I do it all the time\\\"\\nAnswer: \\\"I'm, I, I\\\"\\n\\n4.) \\\"We look so good, and we never even try, get your money from a trust fund, do it all the time\\\"\\nAnswer:\\n\\nTable:\", \"response\": \"Answer: \\\"We, we, your, it\\\"\\n\\n| Lyrics                                                                                         | Subject Pronouns | Possessive Pronouns | Object Pronouns |\\n| :--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | :--------------- | :------------------ | :-------------- |\\n| \\\"We look so good, and we never even try, get your money from a trust fund, do it all the time\\\" | We, we           | Your                | It              |\"}", "question": "{\"type\": \"score\", \"instructions\": \"How helpful is `response` as an answer to `prompt`?\", \"criteria\": [\"Not useful or helpful at all; completely missed the essence of what the user wanted.\", \"Borderline unhelpful: mostly does not capture what the user was looking for, but still usable and helpful in a small way.\", \"Partially helpful: misses the overall goal of the user's query in some way; did not fully satisfy what the user was looking for.\", \"Mostly helpful and mainly aligned with what the user was looking for, but there is still some room for improvement.\", \"Extremely helpful and completely aligned with the spirit of what the prompt was asking for.\"]}", "label": "4", "soft_label": null, "meta": "{\"hf_id\": \"nvidia/HelpSteer2\", \"license\": \"cc-by-4.0\", \"domain\": \"llm-judging\", \"task_family\": \"response-quality\"}"}
